{
  "_about": "The metric library and the cards built from it. This is the only file that decides what the WBR shows. Adding a metric or a card is an edit here, never a code change.",

  "_status": "STARTER CATALOGUE. The shapes are right, the numbers are not. Every target is null and every source ref is a placeholder, on purpose - see _targets below. Each department head corrects their own section once, and then stops touching it.",

  "_targets": {
    "require_targets": true,
    "_why": "The founder asked for accountability against targets. So a metric with no target is not neutral here - it is a metric nobody has committed to. The engine raises a no_target flag for every one of these, naming the department owner. That list shrinking to zero IS the setup process. Set require_targets to false only if you want numbers reported without commitments attached, which defeats the second goal of the meeting."
  },

  "_segments": {
    "_why": "Performance Marketing runs India and US. Rather than two departments, a metric carries a segment and a family. Members of a family roll up to a total, so 'what did we spend' has one answer and 'where' has two. Splitting it into two departments would have made the rollup a manual addition somebody gets wrong."
  },

  "cards": [
